Package: h3-rs
Version: @VERSION@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libcuda1, ffmpeg
Maintainer: apiplant <releases@apiplant.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/apiplant/h3-rs
Description: MiniMax H3 video with stereo audio on NVIDIA GPUs (Rust, CUDA)
 h3 renders text, keyframes or reference pictures, videos and voices to
 an MP4 with a stereo soundtrack, loading the ComfyUI MiniMax H3
 checkpoints as they are. `h3 serve` adds an HTTP API and a built-in
 web UI. Needs an NVIDIA GPU (Ampere or newer) and the ComfyUI model
 files. It links the CUDA 13 runtime (libcudart, libcublas, libnvrtc,
 libcurand), which is not packaged by Debian or Ubuntu: install it from
 NVIDIA's CUDA repository. libcuda1 (installed by the NVIDIA driver
 package) satisfies the driver link only.
